Comparison of Map implementations

HashMap
- Stores key-value pairs.
- Does not guarantee insertion or sorted order.
- Provides O(1) average insertion and lookup.
- Suitable for fast medicine stock lookup.
TreeMap
- Stores keys in sorted order.
- Uses a Red-Black tree internally.
- Insertion and lookup take O(log n).
- Suitable for generating reports in medicine-code order.
LinkedHashMap
- Maintains insertion order by default.
- Provides O(1) average insertion and lookup.
- Suitable for generating reports in the order medicines were added.

Feature	            HashMap	                TreeMap	            LinkedHashMap
Storage order	    No guaranteed order	    Sorted by key	    Insertion order
Search	Average     O(1)	                O(log n)	        Average O(1)
Insertion Average   O(1)	                O(log n)	        Average O(1)
Report generation	O(n)	                O(n)	            O(n)
Best use	        Fast lookup	            Sorted reports	    Insertion-order reports